&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Manager, 3P Revenue Accounting &amp;amp; Reporting to join our Accounting team. You will own revenue recognition, month-end close and reporting for Claude sold through our cloud service provider (CSP) channels: AWS Bedrock, Google Cloud Vertex AI and Microsoft Azure Marketplace. These channels are among the fastest-growing revenue streams at the company. They run on consumption-based, partner-reported data that changes every month.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the accounting point of contact for the finance and partner teams at AWS, Google and Microsoft. Internally, you will partner with Finance, FAB, Engineering and business teams to turn partner billing feeds into accurate, auditable revenue. You will also lead the automation of a close that is still heavily manual. If you want to build the financial infrastructure behind a fast-growing AI company, come join us in our mission to build safe, beneficial AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the revenue close for cloud service provider Marketplace within a listed company timeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prepare and review revenue, revenue-share, reserve journal entries, accruals and true-ups including memos for accounting assessments and judgments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own balance sheet reconciliations, reserves, and the usage-to-invoice-to-cash bridge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Perform monthly and quarterly flux analysis and prepare flux decks for leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own quarter-end deliverables, including footnote disclosures, flux commentary and presentations to leadership and Corporate Accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the primary contact for external auditors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review the work of accountants and contractors, set the close calendar, and keep close packages complete and audit-ready.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own monthly and quarterly 3P revenue reporting for leadership and FP&amp;amp;A, by partner, model, product, region and customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review partner usage, invoice, disbursement and fraud reports each month, and resolve data issues before close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the accounting point of contact for the finance, engineering and product teams and drive reporting improvements that support an on-time close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply ASC 606 to 3P arrangements, including principal-vs-agent, variable consideration and reseller arrangements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Estimate and document reserves, including credit loss (ASC 326).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assess the accounting for new 3P products, programs and billing changes, partnering with Technical Accounting on complex judgments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with the Engineering teams to automate manual close processes, including SQL-driven workbooks, automated reconciliations and system-generated journal entries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own 3P SOX controls, including design, documentation, gap remediation and audit evidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with FP&amp;amp;A, Treasury, AR and business teams on forecasts, cash and partner disputes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have strong ASC 606 knowledge, especially principal-vs-agent, variable consideration, consideration payable to a customer, and consumption-based revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have owned a month-end close with tight deadlines and reviewed journal entries, reconciliations and flux analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have built revenue reporting from large, imperfect third-party data sets and reconciled it to the general ledger.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have managed external partner relationships where you depended on their data, and pushed for fixes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have strong SQL skills (BigQuery or similar) and experience automating close workbooks or reconciliations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have designed or operated SOX controls and supported external audits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communicate clearly with accounting, finance, business and engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thrive in fast-paced, ambiguous environments where processes are still being built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 10+ years of progressive accounting experience, including 3+ years managing revenue accounting or close teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting or Finance; CPA or equivalent (ACA, ACCA).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Big 4 audit experience combined with industry experience at a high-growth tech or SaaS company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with cloud marketplace, reseller or channel revenue (AWS Marketplace, Google Cloud Marketplace, Azure Marketplace).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with usage-based and subscription revenue models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience with Workday Financials, NetSuite, Numeric, Hex or similar close and reporting tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with IPO readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience using AI tools to automate accounting and reporting work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$190,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Anthropic Residency is our paid, fixed-term research program, with placements lasting between six weeks and six months. We are looking for people who have led ambitious work in a variety of technical fields and want to transition to full-time work focused on making sure AI systems are safe and beneficial for all of humanity. If you are a &lt;strong&gt;professor in a quantitative discipline, a technical founder or a staff-level engineer&lt;/strong&gt; and want to transition to work on transformative AI, we want to hear from you. Background in machine learning is not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to expect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A concrete, scoped project matched to your background, with direct mentorship from Anthropic researchers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Claude models and GPU compute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connection to the broader AI safety and security research community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The interview process will include an initial application, recruiter screen, technical assessment, research discussion and a reference check.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applications for this round close on November 22, 2026 (11:59 PM PT). We expect to make offers in January 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are motivated by making sure AI is safe and beneficial for society as a whole&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are excited to transition into working on empirical AI research full-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have led ambitious work in a variety of technical fields (professor in a quantitative discipline, a technical founder or a staff-level engineer)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in fast-paced, collaborative environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can implement ideas quickly and communicate clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience authoring research papers in machine learning, NLP, or AI safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with LLMs, reinforcement learning or Kubernetes clusters and complex shared codebases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentors and research areas&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Potential Anthropic mentors include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/sara-price-310757b2/&quot;&gt;Sara Price&lt;/a&gt;: leads the Alignment Training team; background in data science&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ethanperez.net/&quot;&gt;Ethan Perez&lt;/a&gt;: leads the Alignment Science team; background in machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://evhub.github.io/&quot;&gt;Evan Hubinger&lt;/a&gt;: leads the Alignment Stress-Testing team; formerly at The Machine Intelligence Research Institute (MIRI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=fW7yK10AAAAJ&amp;amp;hl=en&quot;&gt;Samuel Marks&lt;/a&gt;: leads the Scalable Oversight team; background in mathematics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://elanapearl.github.io/&quot;&gt;Elana Simon&lt;/a&gt;: researches the interpretability of language models and biological models; background in biomedical informatics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://belindal.github.io/&quot;&gt;Belinda Li&lt;/a&gt;: researches how language models represent the world, users, and themselves; background in natural language processing (PhD, MIT)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jlindsey15.github.io/&quot;&gt;Jack Lindsey&lt;/a&gt;: leads the Model Psychology team; background in theoretical neuroscience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://nicholas.carlini.com/&quot;&gt;Nicholas Carlini&lt;/a&gt;: researches adversarial machine learning and AI security; previously at DeepMind and Google Brain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sohldickstein.com/&quot;&gt;Jascha Sohl-Dickstein&lt;/a&gt;: works at the intersection of safety and pretraining; background in physics and neuroscience, formerly Principal Scientist at Google Brain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Residents will work on empirical research questions in collaboration with Anthropic&#39;s research teams. Areas we are particularly interested in include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI safety &amp;amp; alignment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scalable Oversight: Developing techniques to keep highly capable models helpful and honest, even as they surpass human-level intelligence in various domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adversarial Robustness and AI Control: Creating methods to ensure advanced AI systems remain safe and harmless in unfamiliar or adversarial scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model Organisms: Creating &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/ChDH335ckdvpxXaXX/model-organisms-of-misalignment-the-case-for-a-new-pillar-of-1&quot;&gt;model organisms of misalignment&lt;/a&gt; to improve our empirical understanding of how alignment failures might arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model Internals and Interpretability: Advancing our understanding of the internal workings of large language models to enable more targeted interventions and safety measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safeguards Research: Developing robust defenses against adversarial attacks, comprehensive evaluation frameworks for model safety, and automated systems to detect and mitigate potential risks before deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Welfare: Improving our understanding of potential AI welfare and developing related evaluations and mitigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI security &amp;amp; frontier red-teaming&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stress-testing frontier models to understand the full extent of their current capabilities in fields such as cybersecurity, robotics or cryptography.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ML systems &amp;amp; reinforcement learning&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving how frontier models are trained and building the infrastructure behind that research, from model architecture, optimizers and training data to accelerator simulators, hardware backends and RL environment pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a fuller picture of the questions we care about, see our &lt;a href=&quot;https://alignment.anthropic.com/2025/recommended-directions/&quot;&gt;Recommendations for Technical AI Safety Research Directions&lt;/a&gt; and recent publications from our &lt;a href=&quot;https://alignment.anthropic.com/&quot;&gt;Alignment&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://transformer-circuits.pub/&quot;&gt;Interpretability&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://red.anthropic.com/&quot;&gt;Frontier Red&lt;/a&gt; teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duration:&lt;/strong&gt; Placements are six weeks, three months or six months, depending on team fit and candidate preferences. Other lengths between three and six months are possible by exception.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This application is for a remote UK position, with the option to work from our London office. However, we prefer that Residents work from our San Francisco office, where most of our research staff is based, but remote participation is possible, especially for shorter placements. Most full-time research roles at Anthropic require relocation to San Francisco. Remote participants need to be based in a country where Anthropic can hire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-time role for the duration of the residency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; £265,000 to £375,000/year pro-rated for the duration of the residency + benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt; We sponsor visas for placements of three months or longer. For six-week placements we encourage remote participation from a country where Anthropic can hire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants may also be considered for the &lt;a href=&quot;https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5183044008&quot;&gt;Anthropic Fellows Program&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
